Modifications: the files were modified. Two upstream skills (2D movement and
physics) were merged into one SKILL.md written fresh in the house style, with
the Godot-side parts of physics-tuning (interpolation, CCD) and GodotPrompter's
physics-system and player-controller recipes condensed into references
(controllers.md, queries.md, bodies-advanced.md). Only GDScript examples were
kept (C# halves dropped). Facts were rechecked against the Godot 4.7 docs and
the 4.4 to 4.7 migration guides and PRs: physics interpolation (2D 4.3, 3D 4.4,
SceneTree move in 4.5), Jolt as the default for new projects in 4.6, the three
4.7 Jolt changes, 4.7 one_way_collision_direction, get_gravity() (4.3+) and
CharacterBody defaults. Fixed on port: the wrong floor_block_on_wall and
"inconsistent jump height" pitfall rows, the delta-less 3D deceleration, the
wall jump whose kick was cancelled by input on the next tick, and the Jolt
single-body joint convention (GodotPrompter had it backwards). Cross-references were renamed to adminhead
plugins (game-feel, game-architecture, godot, godot-shaders,
godot-multiplayer, godot-csharp).
